<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    SL_LairRoom_PowerChamber: the lair's power, drawn from the heat of the deep rock. A
    geothermal generator over a steam geyser and a small battery bank, in a hot, bare chamber
    hewn from the rock. Layout and engine facts in
    Source/1.6/MapGen/Rooms/LairRoomWorker_PowerChamber.cs; the conduits from here to every
    powered building in Source/1.6/MapGen/Utilities/LairPowerNet.cs.

    Geothermal because it needs no fuel and no daylight underground, and is no open flame:
    sanguophages fear fire, and a lair that has to feed a wood or chemfuel burner is a lair
    with servants hauling fuel past the caskets. One generator gives 3600 W; the batteries
    (2400 Wd, full at generation) carry the deathrest rooms through peaks.

    Shapes: 11~13 across and 9~11 deep holds the 6x6 generator with a walking lane all round
    it and the batteries against the side walls; keeping one side under 13 keeps every cell
    within roof-holding reach of a wall, so the generator needs no columns round it. Hewn
    walls and the rock's own floor: it is a service cave, not a room of state.

    Placement: off the beaten path. Never on the axis or a fixed site (anchor Any), pulled
    toward hosts deep in the complex and at least two doors in, often at the end of a
    corridor, and a dead end (no children, no loop doors), so no visitor walks through it.
  -->

  <SanguophageLair.LairRoomDef>
    <defName>SL_LairRoom_PowerChamber</defName>
    <workerClass>SanguophageLair.LairRoomWorker_PowerChamber</workerClass>
    <walls>Hewn</walls>
    <floor>Natural</floor>
    <minDepth>2</minDepth>
    <depthBias>1</depthBias>
    <corridorChance>0.6</corridorChance>
    <corridorLength>3~6</corridorLength>
    <maxChildren>0</maxChildren>
    <allowLoops>false</allowLoops>
    <shapes>
      <li>
        <kind>Rect</kind>
        <across>11~13</across>
        <deep>9~11</deep>
      </li>
    </shapes>
  </SanguophageLair.LairRoomDef>

</Defs>
